Good question — this is a nice ergonomic addition. My plan:

- Add a command-level **`envPrefix()`** (inherited by subcommands). When set, any option without an explicit `.env()` automatically reads from `<PREFIX>_<OPTION_NAME>` (dashes → underscores, upper case). `--port` → `MYAPP_PORT`, `--pizza-type` → `MYAPP_PIZZA_TYPE`.
- Resolve the env var name lazily in `_parseOptionsEnv()`, so the prefix can be set before or after options are added.
- Register the `optionEnv:` listener for *all* options (needed so auto-derived vars work), and report the actual variable name in error messages.
- Allow `Option.env(false)` to opt a single option out of the auto-derived behaviour.

